1
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:51,301
Hope the water's not too cold.

2
00:00:56,848 --> 00:00:58,600
This is my last chance.

3
00:01:42,852 --> 00:01:46,397
Why is it when you need money the most,

4
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:48,149
it's never around?

5
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:50,819
It happens to me all the time,

6
00:01:50,902 --> 00:01:52,987
but that doesn't mean
it's still not depressing.

7
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:08,521
I can't believe how strong he is.

8
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:12,775
Nothing's stronger than money.

9
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:19,199
Well, shit.

10
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:48,603
You know, that's the same look
every super has.

11
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:52,357
Like you really believe
you're something unique.

12
00:03:55,985 --> 00:03:56,819
I love it.

13
00:03:57,320 --> 00:04:00,406
It makes the look I see
in your corpses' eyes

14
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:02,492
so much more invigorating.

15
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:22,470
It's for you.

16
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:28,142
I said it's for you.

17
00:04:45,034 --> 00:04:47,954
You must know this
better than anyone by now,

18
00:04:48,037 --> 00:04:49,247
but money is power.

19
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:50,623
Don't you agree?

20
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:56,462
Who is this?

21
00:04:56,546 --> 00:04:59,507
I'm the chairman of the Mundane Vanguard.

22
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:08,850
In all fights where money is concerned,

23
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:11,144
whoever has more of it will win.

24
00:05:11,227 --> 00:05:13,354
I don't think I have to tell you
who that is.

25
00:05:14,939 --> 00:05:18,026
How about we end the fighting
here and now?

26
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:20,445
All you have to do

27
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:22,989
is sell your power to us.

28
00:05:40,923 --> 00:05:43,134
Take some time
to come up with an offer for the sale.

29
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:45,511
Whatever it is, I'll pay.

30
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:48,890
In the meantime,
let's call a temporary truce.

31
00:06:03,529 --> 00:06:04,864
Since that day,

32
00:06:04,947 --> 00:06:07,700
the Mundane Vanguard
has been eerily quiet.

33
00:06:10,078 --> 00:06:11,788
MY MIN-SUK

34
00:06:14,707 --> 00:06:15,541
Hey.

35
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:16,876
TREAT DEBTORS LIKE FAMILY

36
00:06:17,627 --> 00:06:18,836
Are you almost there?

37
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:21,255
Yes. I'm pretty close now.

38
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:23,966
Remember to ask them
about the formal meeting with my parents.

39
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:26,469
Mm-hmm.

40
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:28,554
How's work?

41
00:06:30,014 --> 00:06:32,266
I'm looking over their books now.

42
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:36,062
It's a total mess.

43
00:06:38,773 --> 00:06:39,857
You sure about this job?

44
00:06:40,441 --> 00:06:42,735
With what they're paying,
of course I'm sure about it.

45
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:44,112
Hang on.

46
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:48,324
Did something happen?

47
00:06:49,992 --> 00:06:51,160
You're freaking me out.

48
00:06:51,244 --> 00:06:52,745
Nah, nothing has happened.

49
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,164
I'll call you again later.

50
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:57,083
-Okay. Bye.
-Mm-hmm.

51
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:18,396
NO ENTRY

52
00:07:18,479 --> 00:07:19,856
FORENSICS
FIRE INVESTIGATION

53
00:07:24,777 --> 00:07:26,279
We'll gather all the evidence…

54
00:07:26,362 --> 00:07:29,240
You there. Make sure
to check the bottom of the pond too.

55
00:07:29,323 --> 00:07:30,700
-Yes, sir.
-Be careful now.

56
00:07:30,783 --> 00:07:31,784
Go deeper out.

57
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:33,619
-Well, Detective?
-Sir?

58
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:34,912
Aren't you getting in?

59
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:39,750
-There you are.
-Oh, hey.

60
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:42,253
-What time is it?
-It's just before 9:00, sir.

61
00:07:43,254 --> 00:07:45,339
Maybe it's time
you replaced that old watch.

62
00:07:47,091 --> 00:07:49,552
And throw out a family heirloom? No way!

63
00:07:50,136 --> 00:07:52,346
Then at least get it fixed.

64
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:54,348
The parts are impossible to find.

65
00:08:09,697 --> 00:08:10,865
Team leader Hwang!

66
00:08:11,616 --> 00:08:12,742
Come look at this!

67
00:08:17,163 --> 00:08:18,331
Right there. Look.

68
00:08:18,414 --> 00:08:19,415
LOAN AGREEMENT

69
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:21,000
-A loan agreement?
-Yes.

70
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:22,793
But look. There's a name written here.

71
00:08:22,877 --> 00:08:24,045
Kang Sang.

72
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:27,298
That says "Sang," doesn't it? Or--

73
00:08:27,381 --> 00:08:31,010
That woman from the hotel fire.
She had a husband named Kang Sang-ung.

74
00:08:32,678 --> 00:08:35,056
KANG SANG

75
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:37,225
You're engaged?

76
00:08:37,308 --> 00:08:38,434
-Yep.
-Oh!

77
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:40,144
This is such wonderful news!

78
00:08:40,728 --> 00:08:43,940
And I was so worried
you'd end up living alone till you died!

79
00:08:45,024 --> 00:08:46,526
Living alone doesn't kill you.

80
00:08:47,443 --> 00:08:49,737
That darling Min-suk is such an angel!

81
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:51,906
I could just die.

82
00:08:51,989 --> 00:08:52,823
Dad, how about you?

83
00:08:53,824 --> 00:08:55,409
I think--

84
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:57,286
Since when does it matter what Dad thinks?

85
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:58,371
Congratulations.

86
00:08:58,454 --> 00:08:59,956
That's right. My opinion is worthless.

87
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:05,920
Ah, so then we should get dinner,
make introductions.

88
00:09:06,003 --> 00:09:07,046
Oh, sure!

89
00:09:07,129 --> 00:09:09,090
We're flexible, honey. You know us.

90
00:09:09,173 --> 00:09:11,509
Just tell her parents to pick a date,
and we're there.

91
00:09:11,592 --> 00:09:13,928
You think maybe we're rushing into things?

92
00:09:14,011 --> 00:09:15,721
Oh, put a sock in it already!

93
00:09:19,934 --> 00:09:22,520
All right. I'll find a day that works,
and I'll let you know.

94
00:09:22,603 --> 00:09:24,689
Oh, I've never been so excited!

95
00:09:26,065 --> 00:09:28,734
I'll go get the rice started.
You're staying for dinner, aren't you?

96
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:29,986
-Okay.
-Good.

97
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:43,207
You need to fill me in.

98
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:47,628
Easy.

99
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:55,052
What is it?
Is there something I forgot to tell you?

100
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:57,138
I can make cash selling.

101
00:09:57,221 --> 00:09:58,556
What do you mean?

102
00:09:58,639 --> 00:09:59,932
The powers I inherited.

103
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:02,226
The Mundane Vanguard.
I have a chance to sell my powers.

104
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:04,478
-Sell 'em?
-Yeah.

105
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:06,355
How would you do that?

106
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:07,398
Huh?

107
00:10:07,481 --> 00:10:08,858
Do you know how it works?

108
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:11,068
How much did they offer?

109
00:10:11,152 --> 00:10:13,029
They said they'd give me
whatever I wanted.

110
00:10:14,113 --> 00:10:17,033
Well, these powers aren't
all that great, I suppose.

111
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:19,243
Anyway,

112
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:21,120
what will you do?

113
00:10:21,203 --> 00:10:23,414
I don't know. Jeez.

114
00:10:25,458 --> 00:10:26,751
Keep in mind,

115
00:10:27,543 --> 00:10:28,544
they're dangerous people.

116
00:10:30,504 --> 00:10:32,923
If you're not careful,
they can hurt you really bad.

117
00:10:34,383 --> 00:10:35,384
Listen, Dad,

118
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:38,262
I need to get something through to you.

119
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:41,932
I was hurting as a kid.

120
00:10:42,975 --> 00:10:45,394
And the one person who caused
all that pain when I was younger,

121
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:48,147
the person who hurt me,
do you have any clue who that is?

122
00:10:48,981 --> 00:10:49,857
Who is it?

123
00:10:53,319 --> 00:10:54,362
Forget about it.

124
00:10:55,154 --> 00:10:57,365
If you don't know, you never will.

125
00:11:03,996 --> 00:11:06,374
They applied for it,
so we can get that done for them.

126
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:07,541
WELFARE COUNSELING

127
00:11:12,588 --> 00:11:14,882
I don't have my ID,
but could I get a copy…

128
00:11:14,965 --> 00:11:19,303
Maybe my Dad's onto something,
and the Vanguard can't be trusted.

129
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:22,682
What if all this is just a mind game?

130
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:25,309
That's my place.

131
00:11:39,657 --> 00:11:40,825
ALCOHOLIC ATTORNEY

132
00:11:40,908 --> 00:11:42,410
Should I ask Attorney Byeon?

133
00:11:42,493 --> 00:11:45,538
Trust me, I know it's tough,
but only you can take them on.

134
00:11:46,872 --> 00:11:50,710
No way. He'd chew me out
for even considering it.

135
00:11:52,211 --> 00:11:54,296
What about Chairwoman Park?

136
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:57,591
Including the cost of the test,
it's 3 billion, 5 million won.

137
00:12:02,012 --> 00:12:02,972
DEBT JEONG-JA

138
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:11,230
That's it.

139
00:12:12,982 --> 00:12:15,025
Out of everyone in my life,

140
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:17,403
there's just one person left to ask.

141
00:12:27,496 --> 00:12:28,956
Welcome. Come in.

142
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:36,839
Guess you started dinner.

143
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:39,633
Here. In case you're still hungry.

144
00:12:42,553 --> 00:12:45,055
I heard they only bake 200 loaves a day.

145
00:12:45,139 --> 00:12:46,974
I went to the mall
on my lunch break earlier

146
00:12:47,057 --> 00:12:49,268
and waited forever in line to buy it.

147
00:12:50,394 --> 00:12:52,772
You think I like bread?
Where'd you get that idea?

148
00:12:55,733 --> 00:12:56,859
I just thought…

149
00:12:57,985 --> 00:12:58,819
Forget it.

150
00:12:59,612 --> 00:13:02,031
You can save them for later
if you need to fight anyone.

151
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:04,450
So I'm supposed to drag
this giant thing around?

152
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:05,367
Not the whole bag,

153
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:07,661
I had them wrapped individually
so you could…

154
00:13:13,667 --> 00:13:15,419
Honestly, there's something
I'm curious about.

155
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:16,337
What's going on?

156
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:20,633
Uh, has anyone sold

157
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:23,010
superpowers for cash?

158
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:27,348
Who told you that?

159
00:13:28,974 --> 00:13:29,809
Huh?

160
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:32,436
Come on, don't play stupid. Who told you?

161
00:13:39,819 --> 00:13:40,653
The Vanguard.

162
00:13:43,197 --> 00:13:44,907
That's what those bastards told me.

163
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:48,994
Everyone except us has sold.

164
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,165
What are you saying?

165
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:55,501
That our friend, Attorney Byeon…

166
00:13:57,628 --> 00:13:59,004
he's known all along.

167
00:14:06,971 --> 00:14:08,556
What are we doing here?

168
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:11,642
You said you were curious
about selling our superpowers.

169
00:14:12,142 --> 00:14:14,019
Well, I just wanna know.

170
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:15,938
Is it even possible to sell them?

171
00:14:16,021 --> 00:14:17,690
Is something like that dangerous?

172
00:14:17,773 --> 00:14:20,234
I know for sure, powers can be extracted.

173
00:14:20,317 --> 00:14:22,194
That guy had Hwa-jin's somehow.

174
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:23,612
Huh.

175
00:14:25,322 --> 00:14:27,241
And who is she, Hwa-jin?

176
00:14:27,324 --> 00:14:29,410
Are you selling or not?

177
00:14:37,501 --> 00:14:38,335
Okay.

178
00:14:39,753 --> 00:14:41,964
You're positive
the answers are in the safe?

179
00:14:53,893 --> 00:14:55,477
Every cent counts.

180
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:01,734
BEOMHA GROUP

181
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:04,528
MISSING SUPERHUMANS LIST

182
00:15:11,869 --> 00:15:13,203
SOLD FOR 400 MILLION WON

183
00:15:13,287 --> 00:15:14,705
PERSUASION HIGHLY UNLIKELY

184
00:15:18,208 --> 00:15:19,960
SUPERPOWER GENE
DISCOVERY AND INHERITANCE

185
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:25,966
SOLD FOR 70 MILLION
SOLD FOR 20 MILLION

186
00:15:27,384 --> 00:15:28,928
SOLD FOR 30 MILLION WON

187
00:15:31,597 --> 00:15:32,723
"Even if not bequeathed,

188
00:15:32,806 --> 00:15:34,850
powers are inherited by children
after death."

189
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:36,101
Wait a minute.

190
00:15:36,185 --> 00:15:39,563
Does that mean I'll pass it down
to my children, no matter what?

191
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:42,274
Yeah. Just like any inheritance.

192
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:48,197
It's a superpower, not a savings account.

193
00:15:49,782 --> 00:15:51,283
LEE HWA-JIN

194
00:15:54,745 --> 00:15:57,081
A SUDDEN BURST OF FIRE
AND EXPLOSIVE COMBAT POWER

195
00:15:57,164 --> 00:15:58,666
SOLD FOR ABOUT 80 MILLION WON

196
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:03,879
I thought she was dead.

197
00:16:08,717 --> 00:16:09,843
I wonder

198
00:16:11,011 --> 00:16:12,846
how come none of them stayed in touch.

199
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:15,641
If I had just barely got out like her,

200
00:16:16,725 --> 00:16:18,477
I wouldn't wanna talk either.

201
00:16:22,356 --> 00:16:24,733
Shit.

202
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:40,749
KANG SANG-UNG, 35, CIVIL SERVANT
POWER: STRENGTH, HEALING

203
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:41,917
SON OF KANG DONG-GI

204
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:43,002
WORTH 1.3 BILLION WON

205
00:16:45,379 --> 00:16:47,756
Low income paired with a desire
to move up in the world.

206
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:50,467
Prevent contact with the Vanguard
at all costs.

207
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:51,844
High likelihood of betrayal.

208
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:20,289
BYEON HO-IN
DIAGNOSIS: HEPATOCELLULAR CARCINOMA

209
00:17:20,789 --> 00:17:22,708
You have to stop drinking immediately.

210
00:17:22,791 --> 00:17:25,502
The chances for recovery are very low.

211
00:17:25,586 --> 00:17:28,255
Have you informed your family
about the results?

212
00:17:32,092 --> 00:17:33,093
Uh,

213
00:17:34,303 --> 00:17:35,637
I haven't. Not yet.

214
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:43,896
You don't have much time left.

215
00:17:44,563 --> 00:17:46,732
You should get your affairs in order.

216
00:18:03,707 --> 00:18:05,250
BANG EUN-MI

217
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:22,476
With food…

218
00:18:25,145 --> 00:18:27,022
you eventually eat your fill.

219
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:30,275
With drink, you eventually get drunk.

220
00:18:35,322 --> 00:18:36,698
There are always limits

221
00:18:38,408 --> 00:18:39,535
to everything.

222
00:18:40,702 --> 00:18:42,579
All things, except for one.

223
00:18:42,663 --> 00:18:44,289
Do you know what that is?

224
00:18:46,625 --> 00:18:47,668
It's money.

225
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:52,214
No matter how much money you have,
you'll never have enough.

226
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:57,803
You reach for it,
but it's always beyond your grasp.

227
00:19:00,764 --> 00:19:03,934
This world we've built
is overflowing with cash,

228
00:19:04,017 --> 00:19:07,437
which means
his powers are potentially infinite,

229
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:09,439
and soon, he'll figure that out.

230
00:19:11,191 --> 00:19:12,025
And so?

231
00:19:12,776 --> 00:19:16,613
So, it's better to buy it now,
even if it costs billions to get it.

232
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:19,116
Look, Dad, I made a mistake.

233
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:21,118
But if you give me a few more days,
I'll be able--

234
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:22,286
I made a call to the US.

235
00:19:26,081 --> 00:19:27,833
He'll be in town by next week.

236
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:37,050
I trust you can handle the final sale
by yourself?

237
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:39,511
Earn your meal at least.

238
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:49,396
Thanks for dinner.

239
00:20:07,331 --> 00:20:09,666
Everyone's dealing with their own issues.

240
00:20:10,334 --> 00:20:11,668
Everyone,

241
00:20:12,294 --> 00:20:14,463
which explains why they do
whatever the hell they want.

242
00:20:16,089 --> 00:20:17,257
My dad does it.

243
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:19,218
So does Attorney Byeon.

244
00:20:20,135 --> 00:20:22,429
Bun-mi, Chairwoman Park,

245
00:20:22,512 --> 00:20:24,514
even the Mundane Vanguard.

246
00:20:44,534 --> 00:20:45,869
Have you made a decision?

247
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:49,831
I'm ready to sell.

248
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:54,795
How much would you like?

249
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:01,802
PRIVATE LOAN, MOM'S POOL, DEPOSIT

250
00:21:01,885 --> 00:21:02,970
TOTAL
4,001,650,000 WON

251
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:09,268
If you're unsure,
I can give you an offer--

252
00:21:09,351 --> 00:21:10,978
4,001,650,000.

253
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:18,151
Shit. Did I ask for too much?

254
00:21:19,194 --> 00:21:21,780
-Done.
-I should've asked for more!

255
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:25,117
As soon as we've prepared everything,

256
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:26,868
I'll give you a time and place.

257
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:39,673
Ha!

258
00:21:40,382 --> 00:21:42,009
Min-suk!

259
00:21:42,509 --> 00:21:45,012
Min-suk! I did it!

260
00:21:45,512 --> 00:21:46,555
Thank you.

261
00:21:48,724 --> 00:21:51,059
Hey, Min-suk. I have a surprise.

262
00:21:52,686 --> 00:21:54,313
-We just had dinner.
-Ta-da!

263
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:58,734
Hey. Don't be crazy.
Why would you buy this?

264
